// This Pine Script® code is subject to the terms of the Mozilla Public License 2.0 at https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/
// Strategy conversion of "FlashGold Continuation v5 - TDI Trade Zone Filter" (© ghostsmartfire, indicator).
//
// FlashGold v5 STRATEGY (XAUUSD build) + FRACTAL DIRECTION FRAMEWORK
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// What is kept from the indicator, unchanged: the bid/ask model from the spread
// input, the TDI direction (RSI -> SMA fast / slow, fast rising = BUY), the
// parent + six child zones alignment filter, the burst gate, the prior-drift
// filter, the entry hold (virtual stop) and the one-entry-per-bar rule. The
// entry price is the indicator's: ask + entry distance for a buy, bid - entry
// distance for a sell, placed as a STOP order.
//
// What the indicator does not have and the strategy adds (all inputs, group
// "S1..S3"): a lifetime for the unfilled entry stop, a stop loss and target in
// ATR or points, an optional trailing stop, a time stop, exit or reversal on
// the opposite signal, a direction filter, fixed or risk-based sizing, a cost
// header (commission = half the spread, slippage), ATR units for the burst /
// entry distance / hold thresholds, and last-closed-bar reads for child zones
// on higher timeframes (non-repainting).
//
// FRACTAL DIRECTION FRAMEWORK (group "F. Fractal Direction Framework")
// From "The Fractal Direction Framework": every regime transition is one
// process at three resolutions - the DIVERGENCE (the warning), the FRACTAL (the
// work: sub-trends testing the parent) and the BREAK (the result). "Trade with
// the parent and use the sub-trend as an entry: the sub-trend gives you the
// pullback, the parent gives you the direction." "You enter on the sub-trend's
// completion, exit on the parent's break." Here, on the "Parent structure
// timeframe" (default 1 hour, read from its last closed bar - no repaint):
//   PARENT     Swing pivots define the parent. Uptrend: each pullback must
//              hold above the last higher low (the protected level, green
//              line). Downtrend: each bounce must hold below the last lower
//              high (red line). Buys only in an uptrend, sells only in a
//              downtrend ("Trade only with the parent").
//   BREAK      A close below the last higher low (uptrend) or above the last
//              lower high (downtrend): the sub-trend exceeded the parent, the
//              old parent is dead and the new one starts ("BREAK" mark). Open
//              trades against the new parent are closed and their pending
//              entry stops cancelled ("Exit on the parent's break").
//   DIVERGENCE Two levels stop agreeing: price makes a higher high while the
//              TDI fast line makes a lower high (uptrend), or a lower low with
//              a higher low in the TDI (downtrend). For "Divergence lasts"
//              structure candles no new entry is taken with the parent ("DIV"
//              mark); a confirming new extreme or a break clears it.
//   FRACTAL    The sub-trend entry: a buy needs a pullback of at least
//              "Pullback depth" x ATR(14) from the latest high since the
//              parent turned up (a sell, a bounce from the latest low). The
//              FlashGold burst that follows is the sub-trend's completion.
//   PERSISTENCE The generalized Hurst exponent h(q) from the structure
//              functions K_q(tau) = mean |dx - mean dx|^q, dx = x(t) -
//              x(t - tau), x = log close, tau = 2, 4, 8, 16, over "Hurst
//              window" structure candles: h(q) = slope of log K_q^(1/q)
//              against log tau. The drift is removed, so H = h(2) above 0.5
//              = memory, persistent (up follows up). The "Hurst gate" lets
//              entries through with H at or above "Minimum Hurst H" (the
//              PDF's reading, the default with the preset off), with H below
//              it (the BTC presets on 1m-30m, 2H and 8H, minimum 0.5), or
//              always (off: the 1H, 4H and 1D presets). The spectrum width
//              h(-2) - h(2) (wide = the flip, maximum disorder) can block
//              entries too (off by default).
// The framework only adds conditions to the strategy's own entries and one
// exit (the parent's break); FlashGold's signal, stops, targets, trailing and
// sizing are unchanged. "Use the Fractal Direction Framework" off, with the
// calibrated preset off (group "P"), the quality filter off and the re-entry
// off = the original strategy, bar for bar, except two reads that no longer
// repaint or overfill: a parent timeframe higher than the chart is read from
// its last closed candle, and fills use the bar magnifier.
// CALIBRATION of the framework and of the whole strategy: see CALIBRATED
// PRESETS below. On BTC/USD the PDF's Hurst reading did not hold (signals taken
// while H was BELOW 0.5 did better), and the divergence and pullback gates did
// not improve the presets consistently: by total return in ATR (the measure
// the exits are ranked by) each helped in sample on 3-4 of the 9 timeframes,
// and in and out of sample only where the presets lose anyway (1m-5m, 30m).
// By average and profit factor the 0.5 ATR pullback gate also helped 4H (PF
// 2.35 vs 1.89 in sample, 1.23 vs 1.22 out of sample) but took fewer trades
// for less total out of sample (30.9 vs 33.0 ATR), so the presets leave both
// off. On a 128-candle window a memoryless market reads H about 0.47 +- 0.08 and a
// persistent one (AR 0.3) about 0.54; the width reads about 0.04 +- 0.08 on a
// monofractal series and its gate stays off.
//
// CALIBRATED PRESETS (group "P", on by default) - BTC/USD, Bitstamp 1-minute
// data 2023-01-01 .. 2026-10-11, one preset per chart timeframe (1m, 5m, 15m,
// 30m, 1H, 2H, 4H, 8H, 1D; other charts take the nearest). Every setting was
// picked on 2023-01 .. 2025-06 only: the most common value among the 60 best
// sets (a plateau, not a single peak), taken from the sets with each of those
// years (2023, 2024, 2025 H1) positive - except the exits on 1m, 5m, 1H and
// 8H, where fewer than 60 sets met that and all sets with enough trades were
// used (the 1m, 5m and 8H presets lose in at least one in-sample year). Then
// it was tested on 2025-07 .. 2026-10. The signal and the quality filter
// never saw that period; the exits did, in part: their ranking rule (step 2)
// was chosen after the first pass's out-of-sample results.
//  1. The signal: parent and zones (chart x1 / x2 / x4, parent x1 / x4 / x8),
//     aligned zones, burst, framework timeframe, trade-with-the-parent, Hurst
//     gate, and the SIGNAL-QUALITY filter (group "Q") - ranked by the
//     t-statistic of the move in the signal's direction over the next 20
//     candles (in ATR). 1m used a reduced grid (parent x1 / x4, 2 aligned
//     zones, no buy cap, no parent-TDI bounds).
//  2. The exits and the re-entry, simulated along the 1-minute path inside
//     every candle with a 0.05% fee per side, ranked by total return in ATR.
//     (TradingView's bar magnifier uses a coarser path - 2-minute candles on
//     15m, 5m on 30m, 10m on 1H-2H, 30m on 4H-8H, 1H on 1D - and only for
//     the last 200,000 of them; with these presets the profit factor moves by
//     about 0.02.) A first pass ranked the exits by the t-statistic; it chose
//     a different stop, target or trail only on 30m, 4H and 8H, and on 4H a
//     tight trail (1/1 ATR, target 4 R: 417 trades, 69% wins) that lost out
//     of sample (PF 0.84) while holding won (1.22). The ranking was switched
//     to total return after that result was seen; the t-ranked presets are in
//     calibration/presets/preset_t_*.json.
// Results of each preset (trades, average per trade in ATR, profit factor;
// in-sample 2023-01..2025-06 | out-of-sample 2025-07..2026-10):
//   1m   7612 / -2.18 / 0.60  | 4043 / -2.83 / 0.54   fees > the move: do not trade
//   5m   3009 / +0.01 / 1.01  | 1637 / -0.43 / 0.82   no edge after fees
//   15m   721 / +0.43 / 1.24  |  379 / +0.66 / 1.39   held up
//   30m   359 / +0.30 / 1.36  |  192 / -0.16 / 0.84   did not hold up
//   1H    720 / +0.28 / 1.23  |  392 / +0.07 / 1.06   weak
//   2H    133 / +0.68 / 1.60  |   77 / +0.14 / 1.11   weak, few trades
//   4H    203 / +0.96 / 1.89  |  134 / +0.25 / 1.22   held up
//   8H     79 / +0.39 / 1.57  |   56 / -0.23 / 0.68   did not hold up
//   1D    138 / +0.25 / 1.50  |   66 / +0.23 / 1.52   held up, few trades
// The table's "Preset" row shows the in-sample / out-of-sample profit factor of
// the preset in force.
// What the calibration found:
//  - REAL MOVE vs END OF MOVE: the quality filter carried over to new data on
//    1m-1H, 4H and 1D, not everywhere. A buy needs the chart's TDI fast line
//    at 50 or above (1m-30m, 2H) and not stretched above 80 (15m, 30m, 2H),
//    and the parent's at 50 or above (5m-30m, 2H); a sell needs the chart's
//    fast line at 40-50 or below (all but 1D) but not already under 30 (1m,
//    5m, 4H, 8H, 1D: the move is spent), and the parent's at 50 or below
//    (5m-8H); on 5m-30m also ATR(14) at least 0.8-1.2 x its 100-candle
//    average (a quiet market's signals fail). Without it every timeframe
//    from 1m to 1H loses; with it 15m and 1H turn positive out of sample (PF
//    1.39 / 1.06 vs 0.63 / 0.94 without) and 4H and 1D improve (1.22 / 1.52
//    vs 1.13 / 1.37). It did not carry over on 2H (1.11 vs 1.13 without it)
//    or 8H, where it hurt (0.68 vs 1.06). On the 20-candle move it was chosen
//    on, it did worse out of sample than open bounds on 15m, 30m, 2H, 8H, 1D.
//  - DIRECTION ACCURACY (no trades, see the FlashGold Direction Filter v1.1
//    and calibration/README.md): the signal's own direction, held until the
//    next signal, is right a little less than half the time on BTC from 5m
//    to 4H (47-49%, buys and sells averaged); the burst more often ends a
//    short move than starts one.
//  - EXITS: in the exit grid no trailing stop beat holding (a 3 ATR stop loss,
//    the parent's break, no target) in sample on any timeframe from 5m to 8H,
//    and holding also won out of sample on 5m, 15m, 30m, 2H and 4H: a trail
//    cuts the trends that pay for the losers. The 1m, 5m, 15m, 1H and 4H
//    presets hold; 30m, 2H and 1D trail and re-enter after the trail; 8H
//    holds until the opposite signal or its 3 ATR stop: its 8 R target
//    (24 ATR) was never reached in 2023-2026, so its re-entry never fired.
//  - RE-ENTRY after a trailing / target exit (group "R"): it helped on 1D
//    (out of sample 15.4 ATR vs 8.2 without) and was mixed elsewhere (over the
//    trail settings tested on 5m-8H it helped both in and out of sample in
//    about 14% of them). Holding the trade is the better way to stay in "as
//    long as the opportunity continues"; the re-entry is there for the presets
//    that trail and for your own trailing settings.
//  - YOUR SETTINGS before this calibration (framework with the PDF gates,
//    parent 4 x the chart, Points exits: stop 5000 / target 50000 / trail
//    4500 / 1000 points = $50 / $500 / $45 / $10 on BTC) lose on every
//    timeframe from 1m to 8H once the fills follow the 1-minute path (1H out
//    of sample PF 0.33; 1D is flat, 20 trades): without the bar magnifier
//    TradingView fills a $10 trail at the candle's best price, which a real
//    market does not give. They stay in the inputs for the preset off.
//  - 1m / 5m: a 0.05% fee per side is 0.1% round trip, about $82 on BTC at
//    $82k: 2.3 x the median 1m ATR ($35) and 0.8 x the 5m ATR ($105) since
//    2025-07, so the fee eats the move the signal catches (15m: 0.4 x). Use
//    15m or above, or the direction filter of a higher timeframe to time 1m
//    entries by hand.
// Set Properties > Commission to your exchange's fee in percent (e.g. 0.05%)
// when testing BTC (the header's cost is XAUUSD's), or the backtest will look
// better than the calibration. The bar magnifier is on in the script (it needs
// a Premium plan).
// (The core calibration below - XAUUSD exports, CALIBRATION.md section 17 -
// is the original FlashGold sweep; the BTC presets above replace it while
// the preset is on.)
//
// EXITS AND SIZING DEFAULTS (S2 / S3, used with the preset off): your settings
// - Points unit, stop loss 5000 pts ($50 at mintick 0.01), take profit 50000
// pts ($500), trailing stop on, activating at 4500 pts ($45) of profit and
// trailing 1000 pts ($10) behind the best price; ATR-mode values 2 / 2 R / 4 /
// 0.2; fixed 10 contracts (oz), max 50.
//
// CALIBRATION (CALIBRATION.md section 17): the defaults below are the
// 60m pick of the FlashGold sweep on OANDA:XAUUSD 10m to 60m exports (2 to 16 weeks), chosen for profit
// factor and win rate with both halves of the export positive. Seconds-based
// child zones could not be swept (no seconds exports): the calibrated zone
// set uses the chart timeframe and its 2x / 4x / 8x multiples, read from the
// last closed bar. Set the chart to 60m and keep the parent = chart.
// 60m: 87 trades, 76% win, +541 per oz, PF 1.93, halves 2.09 / 1.82, max DD 107 per oz. The same settings are positive on 15m (PF 1.23) and 30m (PF 1.34); 10m is flat and 5m loses. Zones = chart, 2x, 4x with 2 aligned.
//
// Data notes:
//  - Child zones on seconds timeframes need seconds bars on your plan; where
//    TradingView has no seconds history the zone returns na. "Ignore zones
//    without data" (default on) drops such zones from the count instead of
//    treating them as MIX, otherwise the whole history before the seconds
//    window would produce no trades.
//  - request.security on a timeframe LOWER than the chart returns the last
//    completed lower bar inside the chart bar (the indicator's behaviour).
//  - Signals are evaluated on bar close (calc_on_every_tick = false), so the
//    backtest and the live behaviour match. The indicator repaints intrabar
//    on the live bar; this strategy does not.
//  - "Points" everywhere = syminfo.mintick units, as in the indicator.
//    Gold: mintick 0.01, so 25 pts = $0.25 = 2.5 pips; the indicator's own point defaults are kept for the Points unit.
//@version=5
strategy("FlashGold v5 Strategy (XAUUSD) + FDF", "FlashGold v5 FDF (XAUUSD)", overlay = true, max_labels_count = 500, max_lines_count = 500,
     pyramiding = 0, initial_capital = 100000, currency = currency.NONE,
     default_qty_type = strategy.fixed, default_qty_value = 10,
     commission_type = strategy.commission.cash_per_contract, commission_value = 0.13,  // USD per oz per side: half of a 2.5 pip ($0.25) spread + $0.6/lot commission (VT Markets)
     slippage = 5,                                                                      // ticks per side. mintick 0.01 -> $0.05/oz
     calc_on_every_tick = false, process_orders_on_close = false, calc_on_order_fills = false, max_bars_back = 500,
     use_bar_magnifier = true)                                                          // fills along a lower-timeframe path inside each candle (Premium plans; TradingView picks that timeframe, the calibration used 1-minute paths); without it a tight trail looks far better than it trades

// ============================== INPUTS (calibrated preset) ==============================
gP = "P. Calibrated preset (BTC/USD)"
presetOn = input.bool(true, "Use the calibrated preset of this chart timeframe", group = gP, tooltip = "On: the settings calibrated on BTC/USD for the chart's timeframe (1m, 5m, 15m, 30m, 1H, 2H, 4H, 8H, 1D; other charts use the nearest one, seconds charts none) replace these inputs: the burst / entry distance / hold (ATR unit), the TDI parent and child zones (chart x1, x2, x4), the parent and zone reads (last closed bar), the framework (structure timeframe, trade with the parent, Hurst gate, exit on the break; divergence and pullback gates off), the exits (ATR unit: stop loss, target, trailing stop), the opposite-signal exit, the entry-stop lifetime (3 bars), the signal-quality filter and the re-entry. Direction, sizing, spread and the visuals stay yours. Off: every input below is used as set. The table shows the preset in force and its tested profit factor. The calibration paid 0.05% per side: set Properties > Commission to your exchange's percentage fee when testing BTC (the header's $0.13 per contract is for XAUUSD).")

// ============================== INPUTS (indicator, unchanged) ==============================
gCore = "FlashGold Core"
spreadPoints          = input.float(25.0, "Spread pts", minval = 0.0, step = 0.1, group = gCore, tooltip = "Full spread in points (mintick units). Half of it offsets bid and ask; the header commission should equal half the spread in price units so the cost is charged.")
entryDistPoints       = input.float(50.0, "Entry distance pts (Points unit)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.1, group = gCore)
entryHoldBars         = input.int(0, "Entry hold bars", minval = 0, group = gCore)
entryHoldMinFavPoints = input.float(5.0, "Hold min favorable pts (Points unit)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.1, group = gCore)
oneEntryPerBar        = input.bool(true, "One entry per bar", group = gCore)

gBurst = "Burst / Direction"
DistUnit         = input.string("ATR", "Burst / entry distance / hold unit", options = ["ATR", "Points"], group = gBurst, tooltip = "STRATEGY ADDITION. ATR: the three thresholds below are read as multiples of ATR(14) of the chart (the calibrated form, portable across symbols and timeframes). Points: the indicator's original point inputs in the Core group are used.")
burstAtrMult     = input.float(0.5, "Burst threshold, ATR mult (ATR unit)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.05, group = gBurst)
entryDistAtrMult = input.float(0.25, "Entry distance, ATR mult (ATR unit)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.05, group = gBurst)
holdFavAtrMult   = input.float(0.1, "Hold min favorable, ATR mult (ATR unit)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.05, group = gBurst)
burstPointsInput = input.float(172.0, "Burst threshold pts (Points unit)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.1, group = gBurst)
useBurstGate     = input.bool(true, "Require burst gate", group = gBurst)
useAnyCombo      = input.bool(false, "Allow any combo", group = gBurst, tooltip = "If on, TDI parent/zone can approve direction even when burst is weaker.")
priorDriftBars   = input.int(60, "Prior drift bars", minval = 1, group = gBurst)
usePriorFilter   = input.bool(false, "Use prior drift filter", group = gBurst)

gZone = "TDI Trade Zone Filter"
useTdiTradeZone = input.bool(true, "Use TDI trade-zone filter", group = gZone)
tdiParentTf     = input.timeframe("60", "Parent obedience timeframe", group = gZone, tooltip = "Used with the preset off. The XAUUSD calibration used the parent = the chart timeframe; the BTC presets use 1 x the chart on most timeframes, 4 x on 2H and 8 x on 30m.")
tdiRsiLen       = input.int(14, "TDI RSI length", minval = 2, group = gZone)
tdiFastLen      = input.int(2, "TDI white fast length", minval = 1, group = gZone)
tdiSlowLen      = input.int(7, "TDI slow length", minval = 1, group = gZone)
minAlignedZones = input.int(2, "Minimum child zones aligned", minval = 0, maxval = 6, group = gZone)
allowNeutralParent = input.bool(false, "Allow trade if parent is flat", group = gZone)
ignoreNaZones   = input.bool(true, "Ignore zones without data", group = gZone, tooltip = "STRATEGY ADDITION. A child zone whose timeframe has no data on this bar (seconds bars outside the plan's seconds window) is dropped from the active count instead of counting as MIX.")
parentNoRepaint = input.bool(true, "Higher-TF parent uses the last CLOSED bar", group = gZone, tooltip = "STRATEGY ADDITION. A parent timeframe HIGHER than the chart is read from its last closed bar, like the zones below. Off = the indicator's plain read: on history it sees the parent bar that closed with the chart bar, live it sees the parent bar still forming, so a backtest with a higher parent does not trade like the live chart.")
htfNoRepaint    = input.bool(true, "Higher-TF zones use the last CLOSED bar", group = gZone, tooltip = "STRATEGY ADDITION. A child zone on a timeframe HIGHER than the chart is read from its last closed bar (lookahead_on + [1] idiom), so history and realtime agree and the backtest cannot see the future. Off = the indicator's plain request.security, which repaints on higher timeframes.")
showZoneTable   = input.bool(true, "Show TDI zone table", group = gZone)

useZone1 = input.bool(true, "Use child zone 1", group = gZone)
zoneTf1  = input.timeframe("60", "Zone 1 timeframe", group = gZone)
useZone2 = input.bool(true, "Use child zone 2", group = gZone)
zoneTf2  = input.timeframe("120", "Zone 2 timeframe", group = gZone)
useZone3 = input.bool(true, "Use child zone 3", group = gZone)
zoneTf3  = input.timeframe("240", "Zone 3 timeframe", group = gZone)
useZone4 = input.bool(false, "Use child zone 4", group = gZone)
zoneTf4  = input.timeframe("480", "Zone 4 timeframe", group = gZone)
useZone5 = input.bool(false, "Use child zone 5", group = gZone)
zoneTf5  = input.timeframe("1", "Zone 5 timeframe", group = gZone)
useZone6 = input.bool(false, "Use child zone 6", group = gZone)
zoneTf6  = input.timeframe("2", "Zone 6 timeframe", group = gZone)

gVisual = "Visuals"
showEntryLabels = input.bool(false, "Show entry labels", group = gVisual)
showEntryLines  = input.bool(true, "Show entry price lines", group = gVisual)
showSideTags    = input.bool(false, "Show right-side price tags", group = gVisual)
priceTagOffsetBars = input.int(5, "Right tag offset bars", minval = 1, maxval = 50, group = gVisual)
entryLineBars   = input.int(20, "Entry line length bars", minval = 1, maxval = 200, group = gVisual)
labelTimeZone   = input.string("America/New_York", "Label time zone", group = gVisual)

// ============================== INPUTS (strategy additions) ==============================
gS1 = "S1. Entry order"
Direction       = input.string("Both", "Direction", options = ["Both", "Long", "Short"], group = gS1)
entryValidBars  = input.int(3, "Cancel unfilled entry after N bars (0 = keep until filled)", minval = 0, group = gS1, tooltip = "The indicator only prints the entry price. The strategy places a stop order there and cancels it if price has not reached it after this many bars.")
allowReverse    = input.bool(true, "Opposite signal may reverse an open position", group = gS1, tooltip = "On: a SELL signal while long places the sell stop; when it fills the long is closed and a short opened. Off: opposite signals are ignored while in a position.")
exitOnOpposite  = input.bool(false, "Close at market on the opposite signal", group = gS1, tooltip = "On: the open position is closed at the close of the bar that prints the opposite signal, before any reversal order.")

gS2 = "S2. Exits"
ExitMode        = input.string("Points", "SL / TP / trail unit", options = ["ATR", "Points"], group = gS2)
slPoints        = input.float(5000, "Stop loss, pts (Points mode)", minval = 0.0, step = 1.0, group = gS2, tooltip = "0 = no stop loss (not recommended).")
tpPoints        = input.float(50000, "Take profit, pts (Points mode)", minval = 0.0, step = 1.0, group = gS2, tooltip = "0 = no target.")
atrLen          = input.int(14, "ATR length (ATR mode)", minval = 1, group = gS2)
slAtrMult       = input.float(2.0, "Stop loss, ATR mult (ATR mode)", minval = 0.1, step = 0.25, group = gS2)
tpR             = input.float(2.0, "Take profit, R multiple of SL (ATR mode)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.25, group = gS2)
useTrail        = input.bool(true, "Trailing stop", group = gS2)
trailActPoints  = input.float(4500, "Trail activation, pts of profit (Points mode)", minval = 0.0, step = 1.0, group = gS2)
trailPoints     = input.float(1000, "Trail distance, pts (Points mode)", minval = 1.0, step = 1.0, group = gS2)
trailActAtr     = input.float(4.0, "Trail activation, ATR mult (ATR mode)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.05, group = gS2)
trailDstAtr     = input.float(0.2, "Trail distance, ATR mult (ATR mode)", minval = 0.05, step = 0.05, group = gS2)
maxBarsHeld     = input.int(0, "Time stop, bars (0 = off)", minval = 0, group = gS2)

gS3 = "S3. Sizing"
QtyMode         = input.string("Fixed", "Quantity", options = ["Fixed", "Risk %"], group = gS3)
fixedQty        = input.float(10, "Fixed quantity (contracts = oz, 100 = 1 lot)", minval = 0.0, group = gS3)
riskPct         = input.float(1.0, "Risk % of equity per trade (Risk mode)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.25, group = gS3, tooltip = "Quantity = equity x risk% / (stop distance x point value). Needs a stop loss > 0.")
maxQty          = input.float(50, "Max quantity", minval = 0.0, group = gS3)
qtyStep         = input.float(1, "Quantity step (rounds down)", minval = 0.000001, group = gS3)

// ============================== INPUTS (Fractal Direction Framework) ==============================
gF = "F. Fractal Direction Framework"
fdOn        = input.bool(true, "Use the Fractal Direction Framework", group = gF, tooltip = "Off (with the preset off): the original FlashGold v5 strategy, apart from the closed-candle parent read and the bar magnifier. The preset turns the framework on. On: entries also need the parent, the divergence, the fractal (pullback) and the persistence conditions below, and trades against a broken parent are closed.")
fdTf        = input.timeframe("60", "Parent structure timeframe", group = gF, tooltip = "The scale the parent trend is read on (its swing pivots, divergence and Hurst exponent), from its last CLOSED candle when it is above the chart: no repaint. One scale above the trading candles is the PDF's parent / sub-trend pair. Uncalibrated default.")
fdPivL      = input.int(5, "Swing pivot left bars", minval = 1, maxval = 200, group = gF, tooltip = "A swing high / low is the highest high / lowest low of this many candles on its left...")
fdPivR      = input.int(3, "Swing pivot right bars (confirmation)", minval = 1, maxval = 100, group = gF, tooltip = "...and this many on its right. A swing is known only this many structure candles after it formed.")
fdTrade     = input.bool(true, "Trade only with the parent", group = gF, tooltip = "Buys only while the parent is up (holding its higher lows), sells only while it is down (holding its lower highs). Nothing while the first parent is forming.")
fdExitBreak = input.bool(true, "Exit on the parent's break", group = gF, tooltip = "When the parent breaks (close below the last higher low / above the last lower high), close the trade on the old side at the next bar's open and cancel its pending entry stop.")
fdDivOn     = input.bool(true, "Divergence warning blocks entries with the parent", group = gF, tooltip = "Uptrend: a higher high in price with a lower high in the TDI fast line. Downtrend: a lower low with a higher low in the TDI. While the warning lasts, no new entry with the parent.")
fdDivBars   = input.int(10, "Divergence lasts, structure candles", minval = 1, group = gF)
fdPullOn    = input.bool(true, "Enter on a sub-trend (pullback) only", group = gF, tooltip = "A buy needs a pullback of at least the depth below from the latest high since the parent turned up (a sell, a bounce from the latest low). The FlashGold burst after it is the sub-trend's completion.")
fdPullAtr   = input.float(0.5, "Pullback depth, ATR(14) mult", minval = 0.0, step = 0.05, group = gF)
HM_OFF   = "Off"
HM_ABOVE = "H at or above the minimum (PDF)"
HM_BELOW = "H below the minimum (BTC calibration)"
fdHurstMode = input.string(HM_ABOVE, "Hurst gate", options = [HM_OFF, HM_ABOVE, HM_BELOW], group = gF, tooltip = "Entries need the parent's generalized Hurst exponent H = h(2) (drift removed) at or above the minimum: above 0.5 the moves persist (up follows up); below 0.5 they mean-revert. On a 128-candle window a memoryless market reads about 0.47 +- 0.08 and a persistent one about 0.54, so 0.5 passes about a third of random windows: set the minimum in calibration (e.g. 0.55). BTC calibration: the PDF reading did not hold on BTC/USD - signals taken while H was below 0.5 (the structure timeframe mean-reverting, drift removed) moved further in their direction than those taken above 0.5, so the presets use 'below' or no gate.")
fdHurstMin  = input.float(0.5, "Minimum Hurst H", minval = 0.0, maxval = 1.0, step = 0.01, group = gF)
fdHurstWin  = input.int(128, "Hurst window, structure candles", minval = 64, maxval = 400, group = gF, tooltip = "Candles used for h(q), with tau = 2, 4, 8, 16. Longer = steadier but slower to react.")
fdWidthOn   = input.bool(false, "Spectrum-width gate (the flip = maximum disorder)", group = gF, tooltip = "Blocks entries while the multifractal width h(-2) - h(2) is above the maximum: the moment the old structure breaks and the new one has not formed. Off by default: the rolling window is far shorter than the thousands of points the PDF asks for reliable spectra.")
fdWidthMax  = input.float(0.5, "Max spectrum width h(-2) - h(2)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.05, group = gF)
fdShow      = input.bool(true, "Show the parent levels, breaks and divergences", group = gF)

// ============================== INPUTS (signal quality and re-entry, calibration additions) ==============================
gQ = "Q. Signal quality (real move vs end of move)"
sqOn         = input.bool(false, "Use the signal-quality filter", group = gQ, tooltip = "What separated the signals that kept going (a real move) from the ones that printed at the end of the move, on BTC/USD in sample (2023-01..2025-06; out of sample it helped on 1m-1H, 4H and 1D, not on 2H or 8H): momentum still building on the chart and the parent (TDI fast line), not already exhausted, and enough volatility. A buy needs the chart's TDI fast line between the two buy levels and the parent's at or above its level; a sell, between the two sell levels and the parent's at or below; both, ATR(14) at or above the ratio x its 100-candle average. The preset sets these per timeframe.")
sqBuyMin     = input.float(0.0, "Buy: TDI fast at least", minval = 0.0, maxval = 100.0, step = 5.0, group = gQ)
sqBuyMax     = input.float(100.0, "Buy: TDI fast at most", minval = 0.0, maxval = 100.0, step = 5.0, group = gQ)
sqSellMin    = input.float(0.0, "Sell: TDI fast at least", minval = 0.0, maxval = 100.0, step = 5.0, group = gQ)
sqSellMax    = input.float(100.0, "Sell: TDI fast at most", minval = 0.0, maxval = 100.0, step = 5.0, group = gQ)
sqBuyParMin  = input.float(0.0, "Buy: parent TDI fast at least", minval = 0.0, maxval = 100.0, step = 5.0, group = gQ)
sqSellParMax = input.float(100.0, "Sell: parent TDI fast at most", minval = 0.0, maxval = 100.0, step = 5.0, group = gQ)
sqAtrMin     = input.float(0.0, "Volatility: ATR / its 100-candle average at least (0 = off)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.1, group = gQ)

RE_OFF  = "Off"
RE_MKT  = "Market, next candle"
RE_STOP = "Stop, close + distance"
gR = "R. Re-entry after a trailing / target exit"
reMode    = input.string(RE_OFF, "Re-entry", options = [RE_OFF, RE_MKT, RE_STOP], group = gR, tooltip = "When the trailing stop or the target closes a trade, the move that paid may still be running: re-enter on the same side while the opportunity continues - the TDI zones, the framework and the quality filter still allow that side (no new burst needed). Market: at the next candle's open. Stop: a stop order at this close + the distance below (a buy) or - (a sell), cancelled like an entry stop. Never after a stop loss, an opposite-signal or a parent-break exit.")
reMax     = input.int(2, "Max re-entries in a row (0 = no limit)", minval = 0, group = gR, tooltip = "Counted from the last fresh signal entry.")
reDistAtr = input.float(0.25, "Re-entry stop distance, ATR(14) mult (Stop mode)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.05, group = gR)

// ============================== CALIBRATED PRESET -> EFFECTIVE SETTINGS ==============================
// The chart timeframe in minutes and its calibration bucket (the nearest calibrated timeframe).
int fgChartMin = math.max(1, math.round(timeframe.in_seconds() / 60.0))
int pTf = fgChartMin <= 2 ? 1 : fgChartMin <= 10 ? 5 : fgChartMin <= 22 ? 15 : fgChartMin <= 45 ? 30 : fgChartMin <= 90 ? 60 : fgChartMin <= 180 ? 120 : fgChartMin <= 360 ? 240 : fgChartMin <= 720 ? 480 : 1440
// preset table, one value per chart bucket (1, 5, 15, 30, 60, 120, 240, 480 minutes, 1D)
int pPm = pTf == 1 ? 1 : pTf == 5 ? 1 : pTf == 15 ? 1 : pTf == 30 ? 8 : pTf == 60 ? 1 : pTf == 120 ? 4 : pTf == 240 ? 1 : pTf == 480 ? 1 : 1
int pMa = pTf == 1 ? 2 : pTf == 5 ? 1 : pTf == 15 ? 1 : pTf == 30 ? 1 : pTf == 60 ? 1 : pTf == 120 ? 1 : pTf == 240 ? 1 : pTf == 480 ? 1 : 1
int pFm = pTf == 1 ? 4 : pTf == 5 ? 4 : pTf == 15 ? 4 : pTf == 30 ? 4 : pTf == 60 ? 4 : pTf == 120 ? 4 : pTf == 240 ? 1 : pTf == 480 ? 4 : 1
float pBurst = pTf == 1 ? 2.0 : pTf == 5 ? 0.5 : pTf == 15 ? 0.5 : pTf == 30 ? 0.5 : pTf == 60 ? 0.5 : pTf == 120 ? 0.5 : pTf == 240 ? 0.5 : pTf == 480 ? 0.5 : 0.5
bool pParent = pTf == 1 ? false : pTf == 5 ? false : pTf == 15 ? false : pTf == 30 ? true : pTf == 60 ? false : pTf == 120 ? true : pTf == 240 ? false : pTf == 480 ? true : false
int pHurst = pTf == 1 ? 2 : pTf == 5 ? 2 : pTf == 15 ? 2 : pTf == 30 ? 2 : pTf == 60 ? 0 : pTf == 120 ? 2 : pTf == 240 ? 0 : pTf == 480 ? 2 : 0
float pBuyFastMin = pTf == 1 ? 50.0 : pTf == 5 ? 50.0 : pTf == 15 ? 50.0 : pTf == 30 ? 50.0 : pTf == 60 ? 0.0 : pTf == 120 ? 50.0 : pTf == 240 ? 0.0 : pTf == 480 ? 0.0 : 0.0
float pBuyFastMax = pTf == 1 ? 100.0 : pTf == 5 ? 100.0 : pTf == 15 ? 80.0 : pTf == 30 ? 80.0 : pTf == 60 ? 100.0 : pTf == 120 ? 80.0 : pTf == 240 ? 100.0 : pTf == 480 ? 100.0 : 100.0
float pSellFastMin = pTf == 1 ? 30.0 : pTf == 5 ? 30.0 : pTf == 15 ? 0.0 : pTf == 30 ? 0.0 : pTf == 60 ? 0.0 : pTf == 120 ? 0.0 : pTf == 240 ? 30.0 : pTf == 480 ? 30.0 : 30.0
float pSellFastMax = pTf == 1 ? 40.0 : pTf == 5 ? 40.0 : pTf == 15 ? 50.0 : pTf == 30 ? 40.0 : pTf == 60 ? 40.0 : pTf == 120 ? 40.0 : pTf == 240 ? 40.0 : pTf == 480 ? 50.0 : 100.0
float pBuyPFastMin = pTf == 1 ? 0.0 : pTf == 5 ? 50.0 : pTf == 15 ? 50.0 : pTf == 30 ? 50.0 : pTf == 60 ? 0.0 : pTf == 120 ? 50.0 : pTf == 240 ? 0.0 : pTf == 480 ? 0.0 : 0.0
float pSellPFastMax = pTf == 1 ? 100.0 : pTf == 5 ? 50.0 : pTf == 15 ? 50.0 : pTf == 30 ? 50.0 : pTf == 60 ? 50.0 : pTf == 120 ? 50.0 : pTf == 240 ? 50.0 : pTf == 480 ? 50.0 : 100.0
float pAtrReg = pTf == 1 ? 0.0 : pTf == 5 ? 0.8 : pTf == 15 ? 1.2 : pTf == 30 ? 1.2 : pTf == 60 ? 0.0 : pTf == 120 ? 0.0 : pTf == 240 ? 0.0 : pTf == 480 ? 0.0 : 0.0
float pSl = pTf == 1 ? 3.0 : pTf == 5 ? 3.0 : pTf == 15 ? 3.0 : pTf == 30 ? 1.5 : pTf == 60 ? 3.0 : pTf == 120 ? 2.0 : pTf == 240 ? 3.0 : pTf == 480 ? 3.0 : 3.0
float pTpR = pTf == 1 ? 0.0 : pTf == 5 ? 0.0 : pTf == 15 ? 0.0 : pTf == 30 ? 0.0 : pTf == 60 ? 0.0 : pTf == 120 ? 4.0 : pTf == 240 ? 0.0 : pTf == 480 ? 8.0 : 0.0
float pTrailAct = pTf == 1 ? 0.0 : pTf == 5 ? 0.0 : pTf == 15 ? 0.0 : pTf == 30 ? 2.0 : pTf == 60 ? 0.0 : pTf == 120 ? 4.0 : pTf == 240 ? 0.0 : pTf == 480 ? 0.0 : 1.0
float pTrailDst = pTf == 1 ? 1.0 : pTf == 5 ? 1.0 : pTf == 15 ? 1.0 : pTf == 30 ? 2.0 : pTf == 60 ? 1.0 : pTf == 120 ? 2.0 : pTf == 240 ? 1.0 : pTf == 480 ? 1.0 : 1.0
int pReMode = pTf == 1 ? 0 : pTf == 5 ? 0 : pTf == 15 ? 0 : pTf == 30 ? 1 : pTf == 60 ? 0 : pTf == 120 ? 2 : pTf == 240 ? 0 : pTf == 480 ? 2 : 1
int pReMax = pTf == 1 ? 0 : pTf == 5 ? 0 : pTf == 15 ? 0 : pTf == 30 ? 2 : pTf == 60 ? 0 : pTf == 120 ? 2 : pTf == 240 ? 0 : pTf == 480 ? 2 : 2
bool pExitOpp = pTf == 1 ? false : pTf == 5 ? false : pTf == 15 ? false : pTf == 30 ? false : pTf == 60 ? false : pTf == 120 ? false : pTf == 240 ? false : pTf == 480 ? true : false
bool pExitBreak = pTf == 1 ? false : pTf == 5 ? false : pTf == 15 ? true : pTf == 30 ? false : pTf == 60 ? true : pTf == 120 ? true : pTf == 240 ? true : pTf == 480 ? false : false
// the preset's test results, 1-minute intrabar fills, 0.05% fee per side: profit factor in-sample (2023-01..2025-06) and out-of-sample (2025-07..2026-10)
float pIsPf = pTf == 1 ? 0.6 : pTf == 5 ? 1.01 : pTf == 15 ? 1.24 : pTf == 30 ? 1.36 : pTf == 60 ? 1.23 : pTf == 120 ? 1.6 : pTf == 240 ? 1.89 : pTf == 480 ? 1.57 : 1.5
float pOosPf = pTf == 1 ? 0.54 : pTf == 5 ? 0.82 : pTf == 15 ? 1.39 : pTf == 30 ? 0.84 : pTf == 60 ? 1.06 : pTf == 120 ? 1.11 : pTf == 240 ? 1.22 : pTf == 480 ? 0.68 : 1.52

// a multiple of the chart timeframe as a timeframe string (above a day: the nearest whole number of days)
// (x1 = the chart's own timeframe string, so it is never mistaken for a higher one; weekly / monthly charts
// multiply their weeks / months)
fgTf(int mult) =>
    int m = fgChartMin * mult
    mult == 1 ? timeframe.period : timeframe.isweekly ? str.tostring(timeframe.multiplier * mult) + "W" : timeframe.ismonthly ? str.tostring(timeframe.multiplier * mult) + "M" : m < 1440 ? str.tostring(m) : m == 1440 ? "1D" : str.tostring(math.round(m / 1440.0)) + "D"

// every setting the preset can replace, as used below (the preset's value, or your input when it is off)
bool   ePre           = presetOn and not timeframe.isseconds   // no calibration below 1 minute
string eDistUnit      = ePre ? "ATR" : DistUnit
float  eBurstAtr      = ePre ? pBurst : burstAtrMult
float  eEntryDistAtr  = ePre ? 0.25 : entryDistAtrMult
int    eHoldBars      = ePre ? 0 : entryHoldBars
bool   eUseBurst      = ePre ? true : useBurstGate
bool   eAnyCombo      = ePre ? false : useAnyCombo
bool   ePrior         = ePre ? false : usePriorFilter
bool   eUseZoneFilter = ePre ? true : useTdiTradeZone
string eParentTf      = ePre ? fgTf(pPm) : tdiParentTf
int    eRsiLen        = ePre ? 14 : tdiRsiLen
int    eFastLen       = ePre ? 2 : tdiFastLen
int    eSlowLen       = ePre ? 7 : tdiSlowLen
int    eMinAligned    = ePre ? pMa : minAlignedZones
bool   eFlatParent    = ePre ? false : allowNeutralParent
bool   eIgnoreNa      = ePre ? true : ignoreNaZones
bool   eParNoRepaint  = ePre ? true : parentNoRepaint
bool   eHtfNoRepaint  = ePre ? true : htfNoRepaint
bool   eUseZ1         = ePre ? true : useZone1
bool   eUseZ2         = ePre ? true : useZone2
bool   eUseZ3         = ePre ? true : useZone3
bool   eUseZ4         = ePre ? false : useZone4
bool   eUseZ5         = ePre ? false : useZone5
bool   eUseZ6         = ePre ? false : useZone6
string eZoneTf1       = ePre ? fgTf(1) : zoneTf1
string eZoneTf2       = ePre ? fgTf(2) : zoneTf2
string eZoneTf3       = ePre ? fgTf(4) : zoneTf3
string eZoneTf4       = zoneTf4
string eZoneTf5       = zoneTf5
string eZoneTf6       = zoneTf6
int    eEntryValid    = ePre ? 3 : entryValidBars
bool   eAllowRev      = ePre ? true : allowReverse
bool   eExitOpp       = ePre ? pExitOpp : exitOnOpposite
string eExitMode      = ePre ? "ATR" : ExitMode
float  eSlAtr         = ePre ? pSl : slAtrMult
float  eTpR           = ePre ? pTpR : tpR
bool   eUseTrail      = ePre ? pTrailAct > 0 : useTrail
float  eTrailAct      = ePre ? pTrailAct : trailActAtr
float  eTrailDst      = ePre ? pTrailDst : trailDstAtr
int    eAtrLen        = ePre ? 14 : atrLen
int    eMaxBars       = ePre ? 0 : maxBarsHeld
bool   eFdOn          = ePre ? true : fdOn
string eFdTf          = ePre ? fgTf(pFm) : fdTf
int    eFdPivL        = ePre ? 5 : fdPivL
int    eFdPivR        = ePre ? 3 : fdPivR
bool   eFdTrade       = ePre ? pParent : fdTrade
bool   eFdExitBreak   = ePre ? pExitBreak : fdExitBreak
bool   eFdDivOn       = ePre ? false : fdDivOn
int    eFdDivBars     = ePre ? 10 : fdDivBars
bool   eFdPullOn      = ePre ? false : fdPullOn
int    eFdHurstMode   = ePre ? pHurst : fdHurstMode == HM_OFF ? 0 : fdHurstMode == HM_BELOW ? 2 : 1
float  eFdHurstMin    = ePre ? 0.5 : fdHurstMin
int    eFdHurstWin    = ePre ? 128 : fdHurstWin
bool   eFdWidthOn     = ePre ? false : fdWidthOn
bool   eSqOn          = ePre ? true : sqOn
float  eSqBuyMin      = ePre ? pBuyFastMin : sqBuyMin
float  eSqBuyMax      = ePre ? pBuyFastMax : sqBuyMax
float  eSqSellMin     = ePre ? pSellFastMin : sqSellMin
float  eSqSellMax     = ePre ? pSellFastMax : sqSellMax
float  eSqBuyParMin   = ePre ? pBuyPFastMin : sqBuyParMin
float  eSqSellParMax  = ePre ? pSellPFastMax : sqSellParMax
float  eSqAtrMin      = ePre ? pAtrReg : sqAtrMin
string eReMode        = ePre ? (pReMode == 1 ? RE_MKT : pReMode == 2 ? RE_STOP : RE_OFF) : reMode
int    eReMax         = ePre ? pReMax : reMax
float  eReDistAtr     = ePre ? 0.25 : reDistAtr

// ============================== PRICE MODEL (indicator) ==============================
pt = syminfo.mintick
halfSpread = spreadPoints * pt * 0.5
bid = close - halfSpread
ask = close + halfSpread
midPrice = (bid + ask) * 0.5

// ============================== TDI DIRECTION (indicator) ==============================
tdiDir() =>
    r = ta.rsi(close, eRsiLen)
    f = ta.sma(r, eFastLen)
    s = ta.sma(r, eSlowLen)
    d = f > f[1] ? 1 : f < f[1] ? -1 : 0
    [d, f, s]

tdiDirPrev() =>
    [d, f, s] = tdiDir()
    [d[1], f[1], s[1]]

isHigher(string tf) =>
    timeframe.in_seconds(tf) > timeframe.in_seconds(timeframe.period)

// plain (indicator) request and the last-closed-bar request; the higher-TF zones pick the second when eHtfNoRepaint is on
[parentDir0, parentFast0, parentSlow0] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, eParentTf, tdiDir(), barmerge.gaps_off, barmerge.lookahead_off)
[parentDirP, parentFastP, parentSlowP] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, eParentTf, tdiDirPrev(), barmerge.gaps_off, barmerge.lookahead_on)
// strategy addition: a parent higher than the chart is read from its last closed bar (no repaint)
parentPrev = eParNoRepaint and isHigher(eParentTf)
parentDir  = parentPrev ? parentDirP : parentDir0
parentFast = parentPrev ? parentFastP : parentFast0
parentSlow = parentPrev ? parentSlowP : parentSlow0
[z1Dir0, z1Fast, z1Slow] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, eZoneTf1, tdiDir(), barmerge.gaps_off, barmerge.lookahead_off)
[z2Dir0, z2Fast, z2Slow] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, eZoneTf2, tdiDir(), barmerge.gaps_off, barmerge.lookahead_off)
[z3Dir0, z3Fast, z3Slow] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, eZoneTf3, tdiDir(), barmerge.gaps_off, barmerge.lookahead_off)
[z4Dir0, z4Fast, z4Slow] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, eZoneTf4, tdiDir(), barmerge.gaps_off, barmerge.lookahead_off)
[z5Dir0, z5Fast, z5Slow] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, eZoneTf5, tdiDir(), barmerge.gaps_off, barmerge.lookahead_off)
[z6Dir0, z6Fast, z6Slow] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, eZoneTf6, tdiDir(), barmerge.gaps_off, barmerge.lookahead_off)
[z1DirP, z1FastP, z1SlowP] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, eZoneTf1, tdiDirPrev(), barmerge.gaps_off, barmerge.lookahead_on)
[z2DirP, z2FastP, z2SlowP] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, eZoneTf2, tdiDirPrev(), barmerge.gaps_off, barmerge.lookahead_on)
[z3DirP, z3FastP, z3SlowP] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, eZoneTf3, tdiDirPrev(), barmerge.gaps_off, barmerge.lookahead_on)
[z4DirP, z4FastP, z4SlowP] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, eZoneTf4, tdiDirPrev(), barmerge.gaps_off, barmerge.lookahead_on)
[z5DirP, z5FastP, z5SlowP] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, eZoneTf5, tdiDirPrev(), barmerge.gaps_off, barmerge.lookahead_on)
[z6DirP, z6FastP, z6SlowP] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, eZoneTf6, tdiDirPrev(), barmerge.gaps_off, barmerge.lookahead_on)
z1Dir = eHtfNoRepaint and isHigher(eZoneTf1) ? z1DirP : z1Dir0
z2Dir = eHtfNoRepaint and isHigher(eZoneTf2) ? z2DirP : z2Dir0
z3Dir = eHtfNoRepaint and isHigher(eZoneTf3) ? z3DirP : z3Dir0
z4Dir = eHtfNoRepaint and isHigher(eZoneTf4) ? z4DirP : z4Dir0
z5Dir = eHtfNoRepaint and isHigher(eZoneTf5) ? z5DirP : z5Dir0
z6Dir = eHtfNoRepaint and isHigher(eZoneTf6) ? z6DirP : z6Dir0

// strategy addition: a zone with no data is inactive when eIgnoreNa is on
zoneOn(bool use, int dir) =>
    use and (not eIgnoreNa or not na(dir))

on1 = zoneOn(eUseZ1, z1Dir)
on2 = zoneOn(eUseZ2, z2Dir)
on3 = zoneOn(eUseZ3, z3Dir)
on4 = zoneOn(eUseZ4, z4Dir)
on5 = zoneOn(eUseZ5, z5Dir)
on6 = zoneOn(eUseZ6, z6Dir)

activeZones = (on1 ? 1 : 0) + (on2 ? 1 : 0) + (on3 ? 1 : 0) + (on4 ? 1 : 0) + (on5 ? 1 : 0) + (on6 ? 1 : 0)
parentSide = parentDir > 0 ? 1 : parentDir < 0 ? -1 : 0

alignCount(dir, useZone) =>
    useZone and parentSide != 0 and dir == parentSide ? 1 : 0

conflictCount(dir, useZone) =>
    useZone and parentSide != 0 and dir == -parentSide ? 1 : 0

mixedCount(dir, useZone) =>
    useZone and dir == 0 ? 1 : 0

alignedZones = alignCount(z1Dir, on1) + alignCount(z2Dir, on2) + alignCount(z3Dir, on3) + alignCount(z4Dir, on4) + alignCount(z5Dir, on5) + alignCount(z6Dir, on6)
conflictZones = conflictCount(z1Dir, on1) + conflictCount(z2Dir, on2) + conflictCount(z3Dir, on3) + conflictCount(z4Dir, on4) + conflictCount(z5Dir, on5) + conflictCount(z6Dir, on6)
mixedZones = mixedCount(z1Dir, on1) + mixedCount(z2Dir, on2) + mixedCount(z3Dir, on3) + mixedCount(z4Dir, on4) + mixedCount(z5Dir, on5) + mixedCount(z6Dir, on6)

requiredAligned = math.min(eMinAligned, activeZones)
parentFlatAllowed = eFlatParent and parentSide == 0
zoneReady = activeZones == 0 or alignedZones >= requiredAligned

tradeZoneBuyAllowed = not eUseZoneFilter or ((parentSide == 1 or parentFlatAllowed) and zoneReady)
tradeZoneSellAllowed = not eUseZoneFilter or ((parentSide == -1 or parentFlatAllowed) and zoneReady)

zoneRiskText = alignedZones >= requiredAligned and conflictZones == 0 ? "LOW" : alignedZones >= requiredAligned ? "MIX" : "HIGH"

dirText(dir) =>
    na(dir) ? "N/A" : dir > 0 ? "BUY" : dir < 0 ? "SELL" : "MIX"

dirColor(dir) =>
    na(dir) ? color.gray : dir > 0 ? color.lime : dir < 0 ? color.red : color.gray

// ============================== FLASHGOLD-LIKE DIRECTION (indicator) ==============================
atrChart = ta.atr(14)
atrPts = atrChart / pt

// ============================== SIGNAL QUALITY (calibration addition) ==============================
// real move vs end of move: the chart's and the parent's TDI fast line and the volatility regime (ATR(14)
// against its 100-candle average). na (warm-up) blocks the side, as in the calibration.
float sqFast   = ta.sma(ta.rsi(close, eRsiLen), eFastLen)
float sqAtrReg = atrChart / ta.sma(atrChart, 100)
sqVolOk  = eSqAtrMin <= 0 or sqAtrReg >= eSqAtrMin
sqBuyOk  = not eSqOn or (sqFast >= eSqBuyMin and sqFast <= eSqBuyMax and parentFast >= eSqBuyParMin and sqVolOk)
sqSellOk = not eSqOn or (sqFast >= eSqSellMin and sqFast <= eSqSellMax and parentFast <= eSqSellParMax and sqVolOk)
burstThrPts   = eDistUnit == "ATR" ? eBurstAtr * atrPts : burstPointsInput
entryDistPts  = eDistUnit == "ATR" ? eEntryDistAtr * atrPts : entryDistPoints
holdFavPts    = eDistUnit == "ATR" ? holdFavAtrMult * atrPts : entryHoldMinFavPoints

burstPts = (midPrice - midPrice[1]) / pt
priorDriftPts = (midPrice - midPrice[priorDriftBars]) / pt

burstBuy = burstPts >= burstThrPts
burstSell = burstPts <= -burstThrPts

priorBuyOk = not ePrior or priorDriftPts > 0
priorSellOk = not ePrior or priorDriftPts < 0

rawBuyCandidate = eAnyCombo ? (tradeZoneBuyAllowed and (not eUseBurst or burstBuy or parentSide == 1)) : (tradeZoneBuyAllowed and burstBuy)
rawSellCandidate = eAnyCombo ? (tradeZoneSellAllowed and (not eUseBurst or burstSell or parentSide == -1)) : (tradeZoneSellAllowed and burstSell)

buyCandidate = rawBuyCandidate and priorBuyOk
sellCandidate = rawSellCandidate and priorSellOk

// ============================== ENTRY HOLD / VIRTUAL STOP (indicator) ==============================
var bool holdActive = false
var bool holdIsBuy = false
var int holdSignalBar = na
var float holdSignalMid = na
var int lastEntryBar = na

float buyEntryPrice = na
float sellEntryPrice = na
bool buySignal = false
bool sellSignal = false

canFire = not oneEntryPerBar or na(lastEntryBar) or lastEntryBar != bar_index

if buyCandidate and canFire
    if eHoldBars == 0
        buyEntryPrice := ask + entryDistPts * pt
        buySignal := true
        lastEntryBar := bar_index
    else if not holdActive
        holdActive := true
        holdIsBuy := true
        holdSignalBar := bar_index
        holdSignalMid := midPrice
    else if holdIsBuy
        elapsedBars = bar_index - holdSignalBar
        holdMovePoints = (midPrice - holdSignalMid) / pt
        if elapsedBars >= eHoldBars and holdMovePoints >= holdFavPts
            buyEntryPrice := ask + entryDistPts * pt
            buySignal := true
            lastEntryBar := bar_index
            holdActive := false

if sellCandidate and canFire
    if eHoldBars == 0
        sellEntryPrice := bid - entryDistPts * pt
        sellSignal := true
        lastEntryBar := bar_index
    else if not holdActive
        holdActive := true
        holdIsBuy := false
        holdSignalBar := bar_index
        holdSignalMid := midPrice
    else if not holdIsBuy
        elapsedBars = bar_index - holdSignalBar
        holdMovePoints = (holdSignalMid - midPrice) / pt
        if elapsedBars >= eHoldBars and holdMovePoints >= holdFavPts
            sellEntryPrice := bid - entryDistPts * pt
            sellSignal := true
            lastEntryBar := bar_index
            holdActive := false

if holdActive and ((holdIsBuy and not tradeZoneBuyAllowed) or (not holdIsBuy and not tradeZoneSellAllowed))
    holdActive := false
    holdSignalBar := na
    holdSignalMid := na

// ============================== FRACTAL DIRECTION FRAMEWORK ==============================
// Generalized Hurst exponent h(q) of the timeframe it runs on: structure
// functions K_q(tau) = mean |dx - mean(dx)|^q over the window, dx = x(t) -
// x(t - tau), x = log close, tau = 2, 4, 8, 16; h(q) = least-squares slope of
// log K_q^(1/q) against log tau (F_q(tau) ~ tau^h(q) in the PDF). The mean
// move (drift) is removed, so H measures memory (up following up), not a
// steady trend. Negative q gets a floor of a quarter of the mean move on every
// move: a negative moment of increments is otherwise set by the single
// smallest move. Rolling sums (cost independent of the window); na until the
// window is full.
// K_2: the variance of the tau-moves (drift removed exactly).
fdK2(float x, int tau) =>
    float dx = x - x[tau]
    float m  = ta.sma(dx, eFdHurstWin)
    math.max(ta.sma(dx * dx, eFdHurstWin) - m * m, 1e-20)

// K_-2: the -2 moment of the tau-moves around their mean, with the floor.
fdKm2(float x, int tau) =>
    float dx = x - x[tau]
    float d  = math.abs(dx - ta.sma(dx, eFdHurstWin))
    float fl = 0.25 * ta.sma(d, eFdHurstWin)
    ta.sma(math.pow(d + fl, -2.0), eFdHurstWin)

// least-squares slope of y against log tau, tau = 2, 4, 8, 16
fdSlope(float y1, float y2, float y3, float y4) =>
    float l1  = math.log(2.0)
    float l2  = math.log(4.0)
    float l3  = math.log(8.0)
    float l4  = math.log(16.0)
    float sx  = l1 + l2 + l3 + l4
    float sxx = l1 * l1 + l2 * l2 + l3 * l3 + l4 * l4
    float sy  = y1 + y2 + y3 + y4
    float sxy = l1 * y1 + l2 * y2 + l3 * y3 + l4 * y4
    (4.0 * sxy - sx * sy) / (4.0 * sxx - sx * sx)

// [H = h(2), spectrum width h(-2) - h(2)]
fdHurst() =>
    float x   = math.log(close)
    float h2  = fdSlope(math.log(fdK2(x, 2)) / 2.0, math.log(fdK2(x, 4)) / 2.0, math.log(fdK2(x, 8)) / 2.0, math.log(fdK2(x, 16)) / 2.0)
    float hm2 = fdSlope(math.log(fdKm2(x, 2)) / -2.0, math.log(fdKm2(x, 4)) / -2.0, math.log(fdKm2(x, 8)) / -2.0, math.log(fdKm2(x, 16)) / -2.0)
    [h2, hm2 - h2]

// The parent on the timeframe it runs on: swing pivots, the protected level
// (last higher low in an uptrend, last lower high in a downtrend), the break,
// the price / TDI divergence and the scaling. Returns
// [parent dir (1 up, -1 down, 0 forming), protected low, protected high,
//  divergence warning in an uptrend, in a downtrend, H = h(2), width].
fdStructure() =>
    float ph  = ta.pivothigh(high, eFdPivL, eFdPivR)
    float pl  = ta.pivotlow(low, eFdPivL, eFdPivR)
    float mom = ta.sma(ta.rsi(close, eRsiLen), eFastLen)   // the TDI fast line
    // the leg's real extreme, confirmed as a pivot or not: the lowest low
    // since the last pivot high, the highest high since the last pivot low
    float loPiv = ta.lowest(low, eFdPivR + 1)
    float hiPiv = ta.highest(high, eFdPivR + 1)
    var float loSinceH = na
    var float hiSinceL = na
    loSinceH := na(loSinceH) ? low : math.min(loSinceH, low)
    hiSinceL := na(hiSinceL) ? high : math.max(hiSinceL, high)
    var float lastH  = na
    var float prevH  = na
    var float lastHM = na
    var float prevHM = na
    var float lastL  = na
    var float prevL  = na
    var float lastLM = na
    var float prevLM = na
    var int   dir    = 0
    var float protL  = na
    var float protH  = na
    var int   divDir = 0
    var int   divAge = 0
    divAge += 1
    if not na(ph)
        prevH  := lastH
        prevHM := lastHM
        lastH  := ph
        lastHM := mom[eFdPivR]
        loSinceH := loPiv
        if not na(prevH) and lastH > prevH
            // a higher high: momentum refusing it is the warning (used in an
            // uptrend), momentum confirming it clears an earlier warning
            if not na(prevHM) and lastHM < prevHM and dir != -1
                divDir := -1
                divAge := 0
            else if divDir == -1
                divDir := 0
        // downtrend: a lower high becomes the protected level
        if dir == -1 and (na(protH) or ph < protH)
            protH := ph
    if not na(pl)
        prevL  := lastL
        prevLM := lastLM
        lastL  := pl
        lastLM := mom[eFdPivR]
        hiSinceL := hiPiv
        if not na(prevL) and lastL < prevL
            if not na(prevLM) and lastLM > prevLM and dir != 1
                divDir := 1
                divAge := 0
            else if divDir == 1
                divDir := 0
        // uptrend: a higher low becomes the protected level
        if dir == 1 and (na(protL) or pl > protL)
            protL := pl
    // the break: the sub-trend exceeds the parent and closes through its last
    // higher low / lower high; the old parent is dead, the new one starts from
    // the leg's real extreme (its last lower high / higher low)
    if dir == 1 and not na(protL) and close < protL
        dir    := -1
        protH  := na(hiSinceL) ? lastH : hiSinceL
        protL  := na
        divDir := 0
    else if dir == -1 and not na(protH) and close > protH
        dir    := 1
        protL  := na(loSinceH) ? lastL : loSinceH
        protH  := na
        divDir := 0
    else if dir == 0
        // the first parent: the first close beyond the last swing
        if not na(lastH) and close > lastH
            dir   := 1
            protL := na(loSinceH) ? lastL : loSinceH
        else if not na(lastL) and close < lastL
            dir   := -1
            protH := na(hiSinceL) ? lastH : hiSinceL
    // the warning lasts eFdDivBars structure candles, the divergence candle
    // being the first
    bool  warnUp = dir == 1 and divDir == -1 and divAge < eFdDivBars
    bool  warnDn = dir == -1 and divDir == 1 and divAge < eFdDivBars
    [h2, width] = fdHurst()
    [dir, protL, protH, warnUp, warnDn, h2, width]

fdStructurePrev() =>
    [d, pL, pH, wU, wD, h2, w] = fdStructure()
    [d[1], pL[1], pH[1], wU[1], wD[1], h2[1], w[1]]

// the structure candle in force: on a higher timeframe its last CLOSED candle
// (no repaint, no look-ahead), otherwise this chart's own candle
[fdDir0, fdProtL0, fdProtH0, fdWarnUp0, fdWarnDn0, fdH0, fdW0] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, eFdTf, fdStructure(), barmerge.gaps_off, barmerge.lookahead_off)
[fdDirP, fdProtLP, fdProtHP, fdWarnUpP, fdWarnDnP, fdHP, fdWP] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, eFdTf, fdStructurePrev(), barmerge.gaps_off, barmerge.lookahead_on)
fdHigher = isHigher(eFdTf)
fdDir    = nz(fdHigher ? fdDirP : fdDir0)
fdProtL  = fdHigher ? fdProtLP : fdProtL0
fdProtH  = fdHigher ? fdProtHP : fdProtH0
// (a bool can be na before the first structure candle: na counts as false)
fdWarnUp = fdHigher ? (fdWarnUpP ? true : false) : (fdWarnUp0 ? true : false)
fdWarnDn = fdHigher ? (fdWarnDnP ? true : false) : (fdWarnDn0 ? true : false)
fdH      = fdHigher ? fdHP : fdH0
fdW      = fdHigher ? fdWP : fdW0

// the parent's break as seen on this chart (the bar its structure candle
// becomes known)
fdFlipUp = fdDir == 1 and nz(fdDir[1]) == -1
fdFlipDn = fdDir == -1 and nz(fdDir[1]) == 1

// The fractal: the sub-trend against the parent since its latest extreme on
// this chart. fdDepth is measured before this bar, so the burst bar that
// completes the pullback is judged on the pullback it ends.
var float fdExt = na   // latest extreme in the parent's direction
var float fdCtr = na   // deepest counter move since that extreme
if fdDir != nz(fdDir[1])
    fdExt := na
    fdCtr := na
float fdDepth = na(fdExt) or na(fdCtr) ? 0.0 : math.abs(fdExt - fdCtr)
bool  fdPullOk = fdDepth >= fdPullAtr * atrChart
// (a new extreme restarts the counter move at that candle's close, the only
// price of the candle known to come after its high / low)
if fdDir == 1
    if na(fdExt) or high > fdExt
        fdExt := high
        fdCtr := close
    else
        fdCtr := math.min(fdCtr, low)
else if fdDir == -1
    if na(fdExt) or low < fdExt
        fdExt := low
        fdCtr := close
    else
        fdCtr := math.max(fdCtr, high)

// the framework's permission for a new entry on each side
fdHurstOk = eFdHurstMode == 0 or (not na(fdH) and (eFdHurstMode == 1 ? fdH >= eFdHurstMin : fdH < eFdHurstMin))
fdWidthOk = not eFdWidthOn or (not na(fdW) and fdW <= fdWidthMax)
fdBuyOk   = not eFdOn or ((not eFdTrade or fdDir == 1) and (not eFdDivOn or not fdWarnUp) and (not eFdPullOn or fdPullOk) and fdHurstOk and fdWidthOk)
fdSellOk  = not eFdOn or ((not eFdTrade or fdDir == -1) and (not eFdDivOn or not fdWarnDn) and (not eFdPullOn or fdPullOk) and fdHurstOk and fdWidthOk)

// ============================== STRATEGY: EXIT GEOMETRY ==============================
atrV = ta.atr(eAtrLen)
// distances in ticks (points) for strategy.exit
slTicksNow = eExitMode == "Points" ? slPoints : (na(atrV) ? na : eSlAtr * atrV / pt)
tpTicksNow = eExitMode == "Points" ? tpPoints : (na(slTicksNow) ? na : slTicksNow * eTpR)

var float lockSlL = na   // locked per pending / open trade, so the ATR at signal time is used for the whole trade
var float lockTpL = na
var float lockSlS = na
var float lockTpS = na
var float lockActL = na
var float lockDstL = na
var float lockActS = na
var float lockDstS = na
trailActNow = eExitMode == "Points" ? trailActPoints : eTrailAct * atrPts
trailDstNow = eExitMode == "Points" ? trailPoints : math.max(eTrailDst * atrPts, 1.0)

calcQty(float slTicks) =>
    float q = fixedQty
    if QtyMode == "Risk %"
        riskCash = strategy.equity * riskPct / 100.0
        stopCash = slTicks * pt * syminfo.pointvalue
        q := stopCash > 0 ? riskCash / stopCash : 0.0
    q := math.min(q, maxQty)
    q := math.floor(q / qtyStep + 1e-9) * qtyStep
    q

// ============================== STRATEGY: ORDERS ==============================
allowL = Direction != "Short"
allowS = Direction != "Long"
inLong  = strategy.position_size > 0
inShort = strategy.position_size < 0
flat    = strategy.position_size == 0

var int placedBarL = na
var int placedBarS = na
bool placedNowL = false   // a fresh signal entry placed on this bar (no re-entry on that side then)
bool placedNowS = false

// opposite-signal handling on an open position
if eExitOpp and sellSignal and inLong
    strategy.close("Long", comment = "opp signal")
if eExitOpp and buySignal and inShort
    strategy.close("Short", comment = "opp signal")

// framework: the parent broke - close the old side and cancel its entry stop
if eFdOn and eFdExitBreak and fdFlipDn
    if inLong
        strategy.close("Long", comment = "parent break")
    strategy.cancel("Long")
    placedBarL := na
if eFdOn and eFdExitBreak and fdFlipUp
    if inShort
        strategy.close("Short", comment = "parent break")
    strategy.cancel("Short")
    placedBarS := na

// long entry: stop order at the indicator's entry price
if buySignal and allowL and fdBuyOk and sqBuyOk and not inLong and (flat or eAllowRev or eExitOpp)
    qL = calcQty(slTicksNow)
    if qL > 0 and not na(buyEntryPrice)
        lockSlL := slTicksNow
        lockTpL := tpTicksNow
        lockActL := trailActNow
        lockDstL := trailDstNow
        strategy.entry("Long", strategy.long, qty = qL, stop = buyEntryPrice, oca_name = "FG", oca_type = strategy.oca.cancel, comment = "FG buy stop")
        placedBarL := bar_index
        placedNowL := true

// short entry
if sellSignal and allowS and fdSellOk and sqSellOk and not inShort and (flat or eAllowRev or eExitOpp)
    qS = calcQty(slTicksNow)
    if qS > 0 and not na(sellEntryPrice)
        lockSlS := slTicksNow
        lockTpS := tpTicksNow
        lockActS := trailActNow
        lockDstS := trailDstNow
        strategy.entry("Short", strategy.short, qty = qS, stop = sellEntryPrice, oca_name = "FG", oca_type = strategy.oca.cancel, comment = "FG sell stop")
        placedBarS := bar_index
        placedNowS := true

// cancel a stale unfilled entry
if eEntryValid > 0
    if not na(placedBarL) and not inLong and bar_index - placedBarL >= eEntryValid
        strategy.cancel("Long")
        placedBarL := na
    if not na(placedBarS) and not inShort and bar_index - placedBarS >= eEntryValid
        strategy.cancel("Short")
        placedBarS := na

// ============================== STRATEGY: RE-ENTRY (calibration addition) ==============================
// A trailing-stop or target exit on this bar (the bar's last closed trade), flat at the close, the side
// still allowed by the zones, the framework and the quality filter (no new burst needed): re-enter on the
// same side. A fresh signal fill restarts the count.
var int reCount = 0
if strategy.opentrades > 0 and strategy.opentrades.entry_bar_index(strategy.opentrades - 1) == bar_index and strategy.opentrades.entry_comment(strategy.opentrades - 1) != "FG re-entry"
    reCount := 0
if strategy.closedtrades > 0 and strategy.closedtrades.entry_bar_index(strategy.closedtrades - 1) == bar_index and strategy.closedtrades.entry_comment(strategy.closedtrades - 1) != "FG re-entry"
    reCount := 0
int reSide = 0
if strategy.closedtrades > 0
    int lastT = strategy.closedtrades - 1
    string lastX = strategy.closedtrades.exit_comment(lastT)
    if strategy.closedtrades.exit_bar_index(lastT) == bar_index and (lastX == "trail" or lastX == "TP")
        reSide := strategy.closedtrades.size(lastT) > 0 ? 1 : -1
reOkL = fdBuyOk and sqBuyOk and tradeZoneBuyAllowed
reOkS = fdSellOk and sqSellOk and tradeZoneSellAllowed
bool reNowL = false
bool reNowS = false
if eReMode != RE_OFF and flat and reSide != 0 and (eReMax == 0 or reCount < eReMax)
    float reDist = nz(eReDistAtr * atrChart)
    if reSide == 1 and allowL and reOkL and not placedNowL
        qR = calcQty(slTicksNow)
        if qR > 0
            lockSlL := slTicksNow
            lockTpL := tpTicksNow
            lockActL := trailActNow
            lockDstL := trailDstNow
            if eReMode == RE_MKT
                strategy.entry("Long", strategy.long, qty = qR, oca_name = "FG", oca_type = strategy.oca.cancel, comment = "FG re-entry")
            else
                strategy.entry("Long", strategy.long, qty = qR, stop = close + reDist, oca_name = "FG", oca_type = strategy.oca.cancel, comment = "FG re-entry")
                placedBarL := bar_index
            reCount += 1
            reNowL := true
    else if reSide == -1 and allowS and reOkS and not placedNowS
        qR = calcQty(slTicksNow)
        if qR > 0
            lockSlS := slTicksNow
            lockTpS := tpTicksNow
            lockActS := trailActNow
            lockDstS := trailDstNow
            if eReMode == RE_MKT
                strategy.entry("Short", strategy.short, qty = qR, oca_name = "FG", oca_type = strategy.oca.cancel, comment = "FG re-entry")
            else
                strategy.entry("Short", strategy.short, qty = qR, stop = close - reDist, oca_name = "FG", oca_type = strategy.oca.cancel, comment = "FG re-entry")
                placedBarS := bar_index
            reCount += 1
            reNowS := true

// protective exits, attached to the entry (also cover a fill on the same bar)
slL = na(lockSlL) or lockSlL <= 0 ? na : lockSlL
tpL = na(lockTpL) or lockTpL <= 0 ? na : lockTpL
slS = na(lockSlS) or lockSlS <= 0 ? na : lockSlS
tpS = na(lockTpS) or lockTpS <= 0 ? na : lockTpS
if eUseTrail
    strategy.exit("XL", "Long",  loss = slL, profit = tpL, trail_points = lockActL, trail_offset = lockDstL, comment_loss = "SL", comment_profit = "TP", comment_trailing = "trail")
    strategy.exit("XS", "Short", loss = slS, profit = tpS, trail_points = lockActS, trail_offset = lockDstS, comment_loss = "SL", comment_profit = "TP", comment_trailing = "trail")
else
    strategy.exit("XL", "Long",  loss = slL, profit = tpL, comment_loss = "SL", comment_profit = "TP")
    strategy.exit("XS", "Short", loss = slS, profit = tpS, comment_loss = "SL", comment_profit = "TP")

// time stop
if eMaxBars > 0 and not flat and strategy.opentrades > 0
    heldBars = bar_index - strategy.opentrades.entry_bar_index(strategy.opentrades - 1)
    if heldBars >= eMaxBars
        strategy.close_all(comment = "time stop")

// ============================== VISUALS (indicator) ==============================
plotshape(buySignal, title = "BUY", style = shape.triangleup, location = location.belowbar, color = color.lime, size = size.small, text = "BUY")
plotshape(sellSignal, title = "SELL", style = shape.triangledown, location = location.abovebar, color = color.red, size = size.small, text = "SELL")

plot(showEntryLines and buySignal ? buyEntryPrice : na, "Buy entry price", color = color.lime, linewidth = 2, style = plot.style_linebr)
plot(showEntryLines and sellSignal ? sellEntryPrice : na, "Sell entry price", color = color.red, linewidth = 2, style = plot.style_linebr)

// framework: the parent's protected level, its breaks and the divergence warnings
plot(eFdOn and fdShow and fdDir == 1 ? fdProtL : na, "FDF higher low (protected)", color = color.new(color.lime, 30), linewidth = 2, style = plot.style_linebr)
plot(eFdOn and fdShow and fdDir == -1 ? fdProtH : na, "FDF lower high (protected)", color = color.new(color.red, 30), linewidth = 2, style = plot.style_linebr)
plotshape(eFdOn and fdShow and fdFlipUp, title = "FDF break up", style = shape.labelup, location = location.belowbar, color = color.new(color.lime, 0), size = size.tiny, text = "BREAK", textcolor = color.black)
plotshape(eFdOn and fdShow and fdFlipDn, title = "FDF break down", style = shape.labeldown, location = location.abovebar, color = color.new(color.red, 0), size = size.tiny, text = "BREAK", textcolor = color.white)
plotshape(eFdOn and fdShow and fdWarnUp and not fdWarnUp[1], title = "FDF divergence (uptrend)", style = shape.xcross, location = location.abovebar, color = color.orange, size = size.tiny, text = "DIV", textcolor = color.orange)
plotshape(eFdOn and fdShow and fdWarnDn and not fdWarnDn[1], title = "FDF divergence (downtrend)", style = shape.xcross, location = location.belowbar, color = color.orange, size = size.tiny, text = "DIV", textcolor = color.orange)

plotshape(reNowL, title = "Re-entry buy", style = shape.circle, location = location.belowbar, color = color.new(color.lime, 0), size = size.tiny, text = "RE", textcolor = color.lime)
plotshape(reNowS, title = "Re-entry sell", style = shape.circle, location = location.abovebar, color = color.new(color.red, 0), size = size.tiny, text = "RE", textcolor = color.red)

makeTimeText() =>
    str.format("{0,date,yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss}", time)

if showEntryLabels and buySignal
    txt = str.format("BUY\nEntry: {0}\nTime: {1}\nParent: {2}\nZone: {3}/{4} {5}", str.tostring(buyEntryPrice, format.mintick), makeTimeText(), dirText(parentSide), alignedZones, activeZones, zoneRiskText)
    label.new(bar_index, low, txt, style = label.style_label_up, color = color.new(color.lime, 0), textcolor = color.black, size = size.small)

if showEntryLabels and sellSignal
    txt = str.format("SELL\nEntry: {0}\nTime: {1}\nParent: {2}\nZone: {3}/{4} {5}", str.tostring(sellEntryPrice, format.mintick), makeTimeText(), dirText(parentSide), alignedZones, activeZones, zoneRiskText)
    label.new(bar_index, high, txt, style = label.style_label_down, color = color.new(color.red, 0), textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)

if showSideTags and buySignal
    label.new(bar_index + priceTagOffsetBars, buyEntryPrice, "BUY @ " + str.tostring(buyEntryPrice, format.mintick), style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(color.lime, 0), textcolor = color.black, size = size.small)

if showSideTags and sellSignal
    label.new(bar_index + priceTagOffsetBars, sellEntryPrice, "SELL @ " + str.tostring(sellEntryPrice, format.mintick), style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(color.red, 0), textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)

// ============================== TABLE (indicator + strategy rows) ==============================
var table tb = table.new(position.bottom_right, 2, 20, border_width = 1)

if showZoneTable and barstate.islast
    table.cell(tb, 0, 0, "FlashGold v5 S", text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(tb, 1, 0, "TDI FILTER", text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(tb, 0, 1, "Parent", text_color = color.gray, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tb, 1, 1, dirText(parentSide), text_color = dirColor(parentSide), text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tb, 0, 2, "Aligned", text_color = color.gray, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tb, 1, 2, str.format("{0}/{1}", alignedZones, activeZones), text_color = zoneReady ? color.lime : color.red, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tb, 0, 3, "Conflict", text_color = color.gray, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tb, 1, 3, str.tostring(conflictZones), text_color = conflictZones == 0 ? color.lime : color.orange, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tb, 0, 4, "Mixed", text_color = color.gray, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tb, 1, 4, str.tostring(mixedZones), text_color = color.gray, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tb, 0, 5, "Z1 / Z2", text_color = color.gray, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tb, 1, 5, dirText(z1Dir) + " / " + dirText(z2Dir), text_color = color.white, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tb, 0, 6, "Z3 / Z4", text_color = color.gray, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tb, 1, 6, dirText(z3Dir) + " / " + dirText(z4Dir), text_color = color.white, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tb, 0, 7, "Z5 / Z6", text_color = color.gray, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tb, 1, 7, dirText(z5Dir) + " / " + dirText(z6Dir), text_color = color.white, text_size = size.tiny)
    // strategy rows
    atrPtsTxt = na(atrV) ? "n/a" : str.tostring(atrV / pt, "#")
    table.cell(tb, 0, 8, "ATR / burst / dist / SL pts", text_color = color.gray, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tb, 1, 8, atrPtsTxt + " / " + str.tostring(burstThrPts, "#") + " / " + str.tostring(entryDistPts, "#") + " / " + str.tostring(slTicksNow, "#"), text_color = color.white, text_size = size.tiny)
    hdrSlip = spreadPoints * 0.5
    table.cell(tb, 0, 9, "Header comm should be", text_color = color.gray, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tb, 1, 9, str.tostring(hdrSlip * pt, "#.####") + " cash/contract (half spread)", text_color = color.white, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tb, 0, 10, "Position", text_color = color.gray, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tb, 1, 10, inLong ? "LONG " + str.tostring(strategy.position_size) : inShort ? "SHORT " + str.tostring(-strategy.position_size) : "flat", text_color = inLong ? color.lime : inShort ? color.red : color.gray, text_size = size.tiny)
    wr = strategy.closedtrades > 0 ? strategy.wintrades * 100.0 / strategy.closedtrades : na
    table.cell(tb, 0, 11, "Trades / win% / net", text_color = color.gray, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tb, 1, 11, str.tostring(strategy.closedtrades) + " / " + str.tostring(wr, "#") + "% / " + str.tostring(strategy.netprofit, "#.##"), text_color = strategy.netprofit >= 0 ? color.lime : color.red, text_size = size.tiny)
    // framework rows
    fdTfTxt = eFdTf == "" ? "chart" : eFdTf
    fdParTxt = not eFdOn ? "off" : fdDir == 1 ? "UP, HL " + (na(fdProtL) ? "-" : str.tostring(fdProtL, format.mintick)) : fdDir == -1 ? "DOWN, LH " + (na(fdProtH) ? "-" : str.tostring(fdProtH, format.mintick)) : "forming"
    table.cell(tb, 0, 12, "FDF parent (" + fdTfTxt + ")", text_color = color.gray, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tb, 1, 12, fdParTxt, text_color = not eFdOn ? color.gray : fdDir == 1 ? color.lime : fdDir == -1 ? color.red : color.gray, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tb, 0, 13, "FDF Hurst H / width", text_color = color.gray, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tb, 1, 13, (na(fdH) ? "-" : str.tostring(fdH, "#.##")) + " / " + (na(fdW) ? "-" : str.tostring(fdW, "#.##")), text_color = fdHurstOk and fdWidthOk ? color.lime : color.orange, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tb, 0, 14, "FDF divergence", text_color = color.gray, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tb, 1, 14, fdWarnUp ? "WARNING in uptrend" : fdWarnDn ? "WARNING in downtrend" : "none", text_color = fdWarnUp or fdWarnDn ? color.orange : color.gray, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tb, 0, 15, "FDF pullback / ATR", text_color = color.gray, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tb, 1, 15, (na(atrChart) or atrChart == 0 ? "-" : str.tostring(fdDepth / atrChart, "#.##")) + " (need " + str.tostring(fdPullAtr, "#.##") + ")", text_color = fdPullOk ? color.lime : color.gray, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tb, 0, 16, "FDF entries buy / sell", text_color = color.gray, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tb, 1, 16, (fdBuyOk ? "BUY ok" : "buy blocked") + " / " + (fdSellOk ? "SELL ok" : "sell blocked"), text_color = color.white, text_size = size.tiny)
    // calibration rows
    pTfTxt = pTf == 1440 ? "1D" : pTf >= 60 ? str.tostring(pTf / 60) + "H" : str.tostring(pTf) + "m"
    table.cell(tb, 0, 17, "Preset", text_color = color.gray, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tb, 1, 17, ePre ? "BTC " + pTfTxt + ": parent " + eParentTf + ", FDF " + eFdTf + ", SL " + str.tostring(eSlAtr) + " ATR, trail " + (eUseTrail ? str.tostring(eTrailAct) + "/" + str.tostring(eTrailDst) : "off") + " | tested PF " + str.tostring(pIsPf) + " / " + str.tostring(pOosPf) + (pOosPf < 1.0 ? " (no edge out of sample)" : "") : "off (your inputs)", text_color = not ePre ? color.gray : pOosPf < 1.0 ? color.orange : color.aqua, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tb, 0, 18, "Quality buy / sell", text_color = color.gray, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tb, 1, 18, not eSqOn ? "off" : (sqBuyOk ? "ok" : "blocked") + " / " + (sqSellOk ? "ok" : "blocked") + " (fast " + str.tostring(sqFast, "#") + ", parent " + str.tostring(parentFast, "#") + ", vol " + str.tostring(sqAtrReg, "#.##") + ")", text_color = color.white, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tb, 0, 19, "Re-entry", text_color = color.gray, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tb, 1, 19, eReMode == RE_OFF ? "off" : eReMode + ", " + str.tostring(reCount) + " of " + (eReMax == 0 ? "no limit" : str.tostring(eReMax)), text_color = color.white, text_size = size.tiny)
